/* Tailscreen — base (English) localization.
 *
 * ONE catalog for all three apps: macOS (Apps/macOS), the GTK app
 * (Apps/linux), the WinUI app (Apps/windows), and the chrome the latter two
 * share (Packages/TailscreenHubUI). A string that appears on more than one
 * platform is ONE key here, translated once — which is the whole reason this
 * file lives in a package rather than beside the mac app.
 *
 * Keys are the English source text exactly as passed to `L(...)` (see
 * ../../Localization.swift). Interpolations appear as printf-style specifiers:
 * %@ for a String/CustomStringConvertible value, %lld for an Int. To add a
 * language, copy this file to `<lang>.lproj/Localizable.strings` (e.g.
 * `sv.lproj`) beside this one and translate the values only — keep the keys
 * byte-for-byte identical. No code changes are needed.
 *
 * Brand names ("Tailscreen", "Tailscale"), key-equivalent glyphs ("⌘Q"),
 * and log lines are intentionally not in this catalog.
 *
 * Section MARKs name the file a key first appeared in; a key used by several
 * platforms is filed under the section that reads most naturally, not
 * duplicated. `LocalizationCatalogTests` is what actually enforces coverage.
 */

